{"name":"Sun Song","hex":"#e9ad17","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sun","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Sundanese."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The star that is closest to the Earth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sun"},{"term":"song","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A musical composition with lyrics for voice or voices, performed by singing.","Any musical composition."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/song"}],"entries":[{"title":"Song Sun","blocks":[{"text":"Song Sun is a Chinese mathematician whose research concerns geometry and topology. A Sloan Research Fellow, he was a professor in the Department of Mathematics of the University of California, Berkeley from 2018 until 2023. In 2019, he was awarded the Oswald Veblen Prize in Geometry. As of 2024, Sun is a professor at the Institute for Advanced Study in Mathematics (IASM), Zhejiang University."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Song_Sun_Berkeley_2022.jpg/330px-Song_Sun_Berkeley_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Song_Sun"},{"title":"Jazz by Sun Ra","blocks":[{"text":"Jazz By Sun Ra is the debut album by Sun Ra. The record label for the first pressing says \"07-12-56\", presumably when it was recorded. The LP originally appeared on Tom Wilson's short-lived Transition Records. In the mid-1960s it was purchased by Delmark Records owner Bob Koester, finally being reissued in 1967."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/58/JazzBySunRa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jazz_by_Sun_Ra"},{"title":"Sun","blocks":[{"text":"The Sun is the star located at the centre of the Solar System. It is a massive sphere of hot plasma, heated to incandescence by nuclear fusion reactions in its core, radiating the energy from its surface mainly as visible light and infrared radiation, with 10% at ultraviolet energies. It is the main source of energy for life on Earth. The Sun has been an object of veneration in many cultures and a central subject of astronomical research since antiquity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg/330px-The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun"},{"title":"Song","blocks":[{"text":"A song is a musical composition performed by the human voice. The voice often carries the melody using patterns of sound and silence. Songs have a structure, such as the common ABA form, and are usually made of sections that are repeated or performed with variation later. A song without instruments is said to be a cappella."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Billie_Holiday%2C_Downbeat%2C_New_York%2C_N.Y.%2C_ca._Feb._1947_%28William_P._Gottlieb_04251%29.jpg/330px-Billie_Holiday%2C_Downbeat%2C_New_York%2C_N.Y.%2C_ca._Feb._1947_%28William_P._Gottlieb_04251%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Song"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/73/SunRaSunSongAlbumCover.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/73/SunRaSunSongAlbumCover.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASunRaSunSongAlbumCover.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Solar_System_True_Color_EN.png/500px-Solar_System_True_Color_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Solar_System_True_Color_EN.png/1280px-Solar_System_True_Color_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Solar_System_True_Color_EN.png/500px-Solar_System_True_Color_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Size comparison of major celestial objects in the Solar System, including the Sun. Distances are not to scale.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASolar_System_True_Color_EN.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Highest_resolution_photo_of_Sun_%28NSF%29_as_of_January_20%2C_2020.jpg/500px-Highest_resolution_photo_of_Sun_%28NSF%29_as_of_January_20%2C_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Highest_resolution_photo_of_Sun_%28NSF%29_as_of_January_20%2C_2020.jpg/1280px-Highest_resolution_photo_of_Sun_%28NSF%29_as_of_January_20%2C_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Highest_resolution_photo_of_Sun_%28NSF%29_as_of_January_20%2C_2020.jpg/500px-Highest_resolution_photo_of_Sun_%28NSF%29_as_of_January_20%2C_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The photosphere is structured by convection cells referred to as granules.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHighest_resolution_photo_of_Sun_(NSF)_as_of_January_20%2C_2020.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/171879main_LimbFlareJan12_lg.jpg/500px-171879main_LimbFlareJan12_lg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/171879main_LimbFlareJan12_lg.jpg/500px-171879main_LimbFlareJan12_lg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thum